# Tasks (KanRite)

A filesystem Kanban managed by the `rite` command.
Status is the folder; `git mv` between columns is the audit trail.

Columns: {% for column in columns %}`{{ column }}/`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
Each task is `{{ board }}/<column>/NNN-slug.md`.

There is one kind of ticket, with fields you fill in as they apply. A
`branch-type`
({% for kind in types %}`{{ kind }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %})
gives it a branch — entering `todo` switches to `<branch-type>/<title>` — and
a ticket without one simply has nothing to check out. `parent` nests tickets
and `assignee` says who's doing it.

Tasks are rendered from a Jinja template. Run `rite templates` to see what's
available, and `rite templates eject ticket` to drop an editable copy into
`{{ board }}/templates/` — anything there overrides the built-ins.

See https://github.com/agile-md/amd
